Well, then, maybe schooner isn't the best choice, either.  I mentioned it
because it's given as an example in the refgrammar text on selbri.

My point is that "spaghetti" is too easy to lojbanize for the example.
It leaves the reader with the notion that, e.g., "rutypitc",
"samymakintoc", and "birjylagr" are good lujvo.

